1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,629
This is OpenKita AI: an open-source,

2
00:00:02,629 --> 00:00:07,265
self-hosted AI assistant for German
Kitas and childcare providers.

3
00:00:07,515 --> 00:00:08,325
Less paperwork.

4
00:00:08,575 --> 00:00:09,680
Better communication.

5
00:00:09,844 --> 00:00:11,055
More time for children.

6
00:00:11,331 --> 00:00:14,688
Kita teams spend hours on paperwork:
letters, minutes, checklists,

7
00:00:14,728 --> 00:00:16,780
and the same questions again and again.

8
00:00:16,985 --> 00:00:19,985
Every hour at the desk is an hour
away from the children.

9
00:00:20,027 --> 00:00:23,376
OpenKita AI is not another Kita
management system.

10
00:00:23,626 --> 00:00:26,816
It is an assistant that eases
existing administration,

11
00:00:26,816 --> 00:00:30,892
designed to integrate with open-source
Kita software such as KitaLux.

12
00:00:31,291 --> 00:00:32,862
Three capabilities are planned.

13
00:00:32,902 --> 00:00:38,049
A Parent Communication Assistant drafts newsletters
and invitations in German and English,

14
00:00:38,049 --> 00:00:41,538
with experimental Turkish and Arabic
that need native review.

15
00:00:41,788 --> 00:00:45,367
An Administration Assistant turns notes
into minutes and checklists.

16
00:00:45,532 --> 00:00:48,900
A Knowledge Assistant answers from your
documents, with sources.

17
00:00:48,976 --> 00:00:51,919
Here is a mock-up of the planned
flow, with fictional data.

18
00:00:51,959 --> 00:00:54,806
The manager asks for a friendly
summer party announcement,

19
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:56,951
with a request for buffet contributions.

20
00:00:57,087 --> 00:00:59,982
The assistant drafts a warm German
text, ready to edit.

21
00:01:00,255 --> 00:01:02,787
Then English, Turkish and
Arabic versions appear.

22
00:01:02,827 --> 00:01:07,901
Turkish and Arabic are experimental: the default local
model does not officially support them,

23
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:09,467
so native review is required.

24
00:01:09,717 --> 00:01:14,611
Every draft is marked as AI-generated, and nothing
is sent until a person approves it.

25
00:01:15,011 --> 00:01:20,202
Version 0.1 is designed to be local-only:
external AI is disabled and fails closed,

26
00:01:20,202 --> 00:01:25,081
there are no child profiles, and a person
approves anything before it is sent.

27
00:01:25,331 --> 00:01:29,846
Planned for version 0.3: audit logs, and a
Privacy Gateway that detects,

28
00:01:29,846 --> 00:01:34,988
minimises and verifies data before anything
reaches an optional external provider,

29
00:01:34,988 --> 00:01:36,556
only after privacy tests.

30
00:01:36,806 --> 00:01:40,545
This reduces risk; it does not
guarantee GDPR compliance.

31
00:01:40,945 --> 00:01:45,871
Everything is open source, licensed under
Apache 2.0: code, prompts, workflows,

32
00:01:45,871 --> 00:01:48,490
schema, API and Docker Compose deployment.

33
00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:50,037
No proprietary edition.

34
00:01:50,287 --> 00:01:53,722
Built with Next.js, FastAPI,
PostgreSQL and Ollama.

35
00:01:53,972 --> 00:01:55,972
Model weights have their own licences.

36
00:01:56,095 --> 00:01:57,200
The software is free.

37
00:01:57,321 --> 00:02:01,785
Revenue comes from services: installation,
configuration, integration, training,

38
00:02:01,785 --> 00:02:03,012
support and migration.

39
00:02:03,262 --> 00:02:07,604
A test installation for one to three thousand
euros is a hypothesis to validate.

40
00:02:08,004 --> 00:02:13,036
One idea is the OpenKita Box, a private AI
appliance installed on premises.

41
00:02:13,286 --> 00:02:18,043
Prices are illustrative hypotheses, hardware
obligations still need investigation,

42
00:02:18,043 --> 00:02:20,189
and we would sell to providers first.

43
00:02:20,589 --> 00:02:23,179
Now the honest part: this is
not yet validated.

44
00:02:23,429 --> 00:02:26,685
Version 0.1 is in progress: the
foundation is built,

45
00:02:26,685 --> 00:02:29,127
and the AI features are in development.

46
00:02:29,377 --> 00:02:33,573
First we will interview five Kita managers,
two providers and two educators,

47
00:02:33,573 --> 00:02:35,009
and ask what builds trust.

48
00:02:35,409 --> 00:02:39,805
The roadmap: version 0.1 is in progress,
then the Knowledge Assistant,

49
00:02:39,805 --> 00:02:44,076
production readiness with the planned
Privacy Gateway, integrations,

50
00:02:44,076 --> 00:02:46,149
and a multi-facility 1.0 release.

51
00:02:46,399 --> 00:02:48,944
Later: Austria, Switzerland
and wider Europe.

52
00:02:49,344 --> 00:02:51,644
Our ask: Kita managers and Träger,

53
00:02:51,644 --> 00:02:55,906
join a thirty-minute interview to help
us validate OpenKita AI.

54
00:02:56,156 --> 00:02:59,314
The code is on GitHub; the link and a
QR code are on screen.

55
00:02:59,509 --> 00:03:00,319
Less paperwork.

56
00:03:00,569 --> 00:03:01,674
Better communication.

57
00:03:01,837 --> 00:03:03,048
More time for children.
